The Fire Chief shall be responsible for and have control over the Fire Department and all fire apparatus belonging to the City, and shall have the following duties:
(1) To properly extinguish all accidental or intentionally caused fires;
(2) To enforce the fire prevention code, Article III of this chapter, adopted by the City Council;
(3) To keep adequate records of all fires, inspections, equipment, fire prevention efforts, and other activities of the Department;
(4) To establish rules and regulations concerning the discipline, good order, proper conduct, care, and management of the Fire Department, subject to approval by the City Council; and
(5) To oversee the investigation as to the cause and origin of all extended or destructive fires occurring within the City limits.
(Code 2005, § 42-33; Ord. of 6-8-2015, § 1(exh. A))
State Law reference— Powers and duties of department, O.C.G.A. §§ 25-3-1 et seq., 25-4-1 et seq.

