(a) The order of plan reviews for new buildings shall be as follows:
(1) Site plan;
(2) Plat review (division of land, where applicable);
(3) Building plan review;
(4) Review of sprinkler plans and other fire protection systems. Plans for sprinkler systems and other fire protection systems, new or modifications of existing systems, shall be submitted to the Bureau of Fire Prevention for approval before construction on said systems commences. This section may be revised at any time deemed necessary by the City.
(b) The order of inspections for new buildings shall be as follows:
(1) Fifty percent inspection as needed for two-hour firewalls and other fire protection systems that will not be visible at the 80 percent inspection.
(2) Eighty percent inspection to inspect firewalls, sprinkler piping, insulation and other fire protection system not visible at final inspection.
(3) Final fire inspection; results are forwarded to the Building Official for the issuance of the certificate of occupancy pending the completion of all other required inspections.
(Code 2005, § 42-77; Ord. of 6-8-2015, § 1(exh. A))
